{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith","id":1552317,"title":"The Remembered Dead as a Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-12T18:36:05-07:00","id":1552317,"title":"The Remembered Dead as a Kith","content":"Pixar's <b>Coco.</b> The Remembered dead as a kith seems workable. Childling, Wilder, or Gump, would be decided by age at death combined with life attitude. Some people would be Childlings at 90! They'd have the memories and skills they had in life and would last as long as they are remembered. <br /> <br /> Still, although the time limit and restrictions of movement are Frailities, what are the Brithrights and how to define them?<br /> <br /> Opinions? Reactions? Ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T18:59:15-07:00","id":1552320,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen that movie, but that kind of reminds me of the Keremet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-12T19:53:41-07:00","id":1552321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1552320#post1552320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen that movie, but that kind of reminds me of the Keremet</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a similarity, but the Keremet are without emotions. The Keremet are very different beings. The lively sassy Remembered Dead of Coco are wildly distinct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T00:31:06-07:00","id":1552355,"title":"","content":"The problem is metaphysics. The dead have a well established place in the WoD, and Changeling doesn't changes it. Being a Kith means being a Fae, not a deceased spirit, even because it means undergoing the Changeling Way. Also, the game takes place in the Dreaming and the Material, not in the &quot;Lando of the Dead&quot;, you have to consider what bringing those dead people to the Material entails.<br /> <br /> Overall the idea would require a lot of work and change to fit. Are they Changelings that just resemble dead people? Are they dead people that somehow became fae? If so, do they go through the Changeling Way, taking the place of a human soul in a new body? Do they just live in the Dreaming, in some sort of stable realm? How this place even exists, and where?<br /> <br /> In the end, the Remembered Dead as they are in the movie rely in a cosmological concept that isn't easily applicable in the WoD, much less in Changeling: that the destination of a human soul isn't a mystery. In the WoD souls only go to known destinations when things go horribly wrong, or at least very weird. So to have the Remembered Dead as they are in the movie you would have to either make it an extremely specific and extraordinary thing happening, maybe something that's only happening at a given region, or you have to fundamentally change the setting (which is perfectly doable and may still use the same rules).<br /> <br /> Everything depends on how you want to answer those questions, what you want the Remembered Dead to be in your game. The best answer may be one in a variety of different Birthrights, it may be to conceptually change Changelings for Remembered Dead and use all Kiths for them, it may be to use another Gallain, to create a new Gallain, to use other splat as basis, or even to look for other games.<br /> <br /> By the way: the concept of the Remembered Dead is more closely followed in the Chronicles of Darkness, especially in <b>Geist: the Sin-Eaters</b>. It is all about the Remembered Dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T22:00:04-07:00","id":1552401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1552355#post1552355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is metaphysics. The dead have a well established place in the WoD, and Changeling doesn't changes it. Being a Kith means being a Fae, not a deceased spirit, even because it means undergoing the Changeling Way. Also, the game takes place in the Dreaming and the Material, not in the &quot;Lando of the Dead&quot;, you have to consider what bringing those dead people to the Material entails.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might not be as big of an issue as you might think. There are the Gallain, which include the Nunnehi, a group of &quot;fae&quot; that are more closely associated with the spirit world than with the Dreaming. And there are Dark Kin, who lack a physical form and maintain an ephemeral existence. Combine the two with a focus on the Lower Umbra instead of the Middle Umbra, and you might have something. <br /> <br /> With that said, I <i>do</i> wonder why the OP didn't start with Wraith or Orpheus; that would certainly be a better fit. Orpheus in particular is more compatible with Remembered Dead concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T05:56:07-07:00","id":1552407,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind also that the vast majority of people that die don't become wraiths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T09:01:08-07:00","id":1552415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1552401#post1552401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are the Gallain</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that, the problem of metaphysics is specifically for the idea of them as a Kith. I particularly think that, while Wraith/Orpheus is definitely the best place to start at least to define what those things are and where they live, as far as the apparent intention of the OP goes the simplest option is to make a new Gallain based on the Dark Kin.<br /> <br /> But yeah, while I get that the <i>D\u00eda de Los Muertos</i> vibe seems to mesh well with Changeling, their concept don't really belong there. The best option is to take the spirit of the setting and transport it to Wraith/Orpheus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1552407#post1552407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep in mind also that the vast majority of people that die don't become wraiths</div> </div> </div> </div>The Remembered Dead don't fit WoD's definition of a Wraith, and the difference is key to the OP's proposal.<br /> <br /> Whatever splat <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar857_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"857\" data-vbnamecard=\"857\">Astromancer</a> decides to use as starting point, the Remembered Dead will be exceptional within the setting. They're not troubled spirits, they're specifically not ghosts, and they're usually (if not necessarily) content with their lot. They're every dead person who's still remembered by the living (hence the name) and mostly continue their lives in their realm, but without physical necessities. It's a very different proposal from a typical Wraith regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T03:41:41-07:00","id":1552446,"title":"","content":"Monteparnas points out the whole <i>D\u00eca de Los Muertos </i>vibe fits Changeling in a way it simply doesn't fit Wraith/Orpheus or Geist. I went with mood not metaphysics. (Can anyone clearly define Metaphysics in a sentence or two?) <br /> <br /> The Remembered Dead don't interact in the predatory ways that other dead/undead do. They seem to live on the glamor of memory and love. They're certainly kith adjacent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T10:28:27-07:00","id":1552452,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, <b>Geist</b> specifically cites <i>Coco</i> as an inspiration for the Absent (the playable ghosts described in its first Appendix), the generally upbeat tone as something that krewes strive to create, and the shantytown section as a good representation of the existing River Cities of the setting. There's a Wake Merit that gives the Absent a regular influx of Essence from those living who remember them, and the Memories Trait that the Absent have functions a bit like gathering Glamour does for changelings, with Harvesting Memories being similar to Ravaging while Making Memories is a bit like Reverie. <br /> <br /> A krewe could easily be built around fostering interactions between its living members and its dead members, so that the option to Make Memories becomes more readily available, making the &quot;lives&quot; of that krewe's Absent less of a hustle and more comfortable. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> I wasn't going to mention it at first, as it's a CoD gameline and this discussion involves the WoD setting. But if the argument is solely that <b>Geist</b> doesn't fit the <i>D\u00eca de Los Muertos</i> vibe, I have to push back on that. And while <b>Orpheus</b> doesn't fit the vibe quite as well as <b>Geist</b> does, it wouldn't take much to tweak it so that it does. The main thing lacking is that the Spirits of the Dead don't have much of a dependence on the memories of the living. Frankly, changing it so that they do solves a bit of a plot hole in <b>Orpheus</b>: the corporation employs ghosts; but how does it pay them? Introducing something like the Absent's use of Memories as a currency resolves that issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-16T15:54:31-07:00","id":1552464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1552446#post1552446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Monteparnas points out the whole <i>D\u00eca de Los Muertos </i>vibe fits Changeling in a way it simply doesn't fit Wraith/Orpheus or Geist. I went with mood not metaphysics. (Can anyone clearly define Metaphysics in a sentence or two?)<br /> <br /> The Remembered Dead don't interact in the predatory ways that other dead/undead do. They seem to live on the glamor of memory and love. They're certainly kith adjacent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't said it doesn't fit <b>Geist</b>. It fits <b>Geist</b> better than any other gameline cited in this thread (and seriously more than any gameline in either WoD or CofD). <b>Geist</b> is precisely built over similar cosmologies, the very trait that makes this hard to pull at <b>Wraith</b>.<br /> <br /> Metaphysics could be understood here as the physics/cosmology of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> The problem with the whole idea is that it has nothing to do with how the dead work in the setting or how Changelings work in the setting. Changelings aren't dead people. They aren't simply spirits. They're fairies from a specific reality called the Dreaming, incarnated in human bodies. How do you fit the Remembered Dead into this? What are they in the setting.<br /> <br /> And Glamour isn't something exclusive to the Changelings. What do you think a Kith is? A lot of other entities in the Dreaming (and even some outside of it) use Glamour. Making a <b>Wraith-Adjacent</b> entity that gathers and uses Glamour is perfectly doable (tricky, but doable), and makes a lot more sense. Making a place that for some unknown reason attracts the souls of the dead to the Dreaming and make them into a new kind of Gallain (entities from the Dreaming that usually use Glamour) is also doable and makes more sense.<br /> <br /> Not to say that you don't really need Glamour to do anything they do in <i>Coco</i>. This is about mood and inclination, not about what kind of preternatural energy you feed from. The Dreaming is a place of creativity and chaos, not memories. Whimsy and joy are just regular (not mandatory) side effects, but they can happen at other places, for other reasons.<br /> <br /> You didn't addressed any of my questions in my first post, you could start there. You have to define what those entities are in the setting, and what they are not. Once that's done, then we can say for sure if they make any sense as a Kith, or if there are better options to make them. But as they are in the movie, then they're definitely not Changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-14T19:53:39-07:00","id":1553191,"title":"","content":"Random thought. In Mummy: the Resurrection, the different types of mummy correspond to which of your five souls the ancient mummy spirit bonded to / replaced (usually supplementing whichever of yours was most flawed/deficient during your life). So what if a fae spirit similarly filled in a missing piece, rather than the whole soul, on death rather thn birth? Setting aside for a moment just what would have to go wrong for this to happen.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-15T10:27:48-07:00","id":1553205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1553191#post1553191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random thought. In Mummy: the Resurrection, the different types of mummy correspond to which of your five souls the ancient mummy spirit bonded to / replaced (usually supplementing whichever of yours was most flawed/deficient during your life). So what if a fae spirit similarly filled in a missing piece, rather than the whole soul, on death rather thn birth? Setting aside for a moment just what would have to go wrong for this to happen.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea. Since I can't think of a reason for a fae to do this on purpose, the most probable cause would be a failed Changeling Way ritual.<br /> <br /> Now, usually it's understood that Wraiths don't have the full set of souls, only two IIRC (one becoming the main Wraith and the other the Shadow). If this keeps the souls from scattering, the resulting being wouldn't be a Wraith, it would be a more whole entity. Maybe something similar in fact to a Mummy. Maybe it happened with a Changeling performing the Way near the Spell of Life?<br /> <br /> An option would be for a Changeling to do so as a means to save a mortal's life. There are many potential ways to both justify and stat such a creature, that's a very interesting idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T13:44:06-07:00","id":1561317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1553205#post1553205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting idea. Since I can't think of a reason for a fae to do this on purpose, the most probable cause would be a failed Changeling Way ritual.<br /> <br /> Now, usually it's understood that Wraiths don't have the full set of souls, only two IIRC (one becoming the main Wraith and the other the Shadow). If this keeps the souls from scattering, the resulting being wouldn't be a Wraith, it would be a more whole entity. Maybe something similar in fact to a Mummy. Maybe it happened with a Changeling performing the Way near the Spell of Life?<br /> <br /> An option would be for a Changeling to do so as a means to save a mortal's life. There are many potential ways to both justify and stat such a creature, that's a very interesting idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a failed attempt to replicate the Spell of Life using the Naming Art could do this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T14:57:06-07:00","id":1561320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1552317-the-remembered-dead-as-a-kith?p=1561317#post1561317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe a failed attempt to replicate the Spell of Life using the Naming Art could do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be possible, but overkill.<br /> <br /> All Changelings know how to possess a human body. While there's no rules for doing this in game, that's what the Arcadian Sidhe do to get a human life and endure Banality. They also all know how to do the ritual of the Changeling Way, that is already a soul fusion.<br /> <br /> Probably a simple research in the Dreaming, or a Quest at worse, would do the trick and weld the Changeling spirit into the slot, saving the mortal and creating whatever comes from this.<br /> <br /> Using Naming would add complications and a greater influence of the Changeling into the result, which is just as interesting but I'd say not the same thing. Would rather depend on how Naming was used, on which names.<br /> <br /> In theory, to do it with an Art even Wayfare would do. Each Art would inform what sorts of shenanigans the ST will add to the result rather than be a rigid requisit. Changeling doesn't mesh well with rigid nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}